\f4\fs26 Sarah had been enduring nightmares every night for weeks. The imagery was not grotesque or even of itself frightening, but the underlying mood of the dream was a combination of angst, horror and impending doom. When she woke she was unable to nail down any specific narrative, recalling only one image each morning, burnt into her brain. A strange pattern that was oddly familiar, but she was unable to place I, but it stuck-fast. Being possessed of a sturdy mind, she had never experienced fear on such scale and was ignorant of the overwhelming power of the sub-conscious and its ability to identify, precisely, what will frighten the shit out of you. Outwardly, it did not take long for her to return to her natural serene state of being, but as the days turned into weeks and her unconscious mind refused mercy, her resolve began to erode incrementally. She had not bothered to mention the nocturnal torture to Dr Logan on her weekly visits, dismissing it as inconsequential, but would do so at the next appointment later that day. \
\'93Hey Sarah, or should I say Blessed Mother?\'94 Dr Logan, the Holy Aunt, gushed as Sarah motioned her into her palatial apartment. \'93Pregnancy really suits, you are radiant!\'94\
\'93You look fantastic, too.\'94 Sarah noted Dr Logan was positively glowing these days and could quite rightly be regarded as beautiful. \'93What is your secret?\'94 She hoped it wasn\'92t the same as her own, but it was.\
 \'93Good clean living. Ha, Ha.\'94 She giggled again and then looked around, \'93I never cease to be amazed by your apartment. This place is spectacular. How many bedrooms?\'94\
\'93Four, plus a games room I could make into a bedroom if the need ever arose.\'94 Sarah was house-proud, but did not feel like doing the tour. There were bigger issues to tackle.\
\'93Where do you want to do this, Kathy?\'94\
\'93Same as last week. Massage table in in the lounge area. I love looking out that window. I want to speak to you about some data I have been receiving from the abdominal patch.\'94 She broke out a small electronic device that projected a tiny holo-screen. \'93For the past several weeks I have noted that while you are sleeping, usually between the hours of 2.00am and 5.00am, you and the baby\'92s heart rating rises rapidly, and remains your blood pressure becomes dangerously high.\'94 She helped Sarah on to the table and gently laid her flat and prodded the little pot-belly Sarah had begun growing. \
\'93Dangerously high? I am just having a few nightmares.\'94\
\'93Every night for the past several weeks?\'94 Kathy countered.\
\'93Yes, it is really quite annoying.\'94 Sarah placed her hand on her tiny round abdomen, still barely showing. \'93Just thinking about it bothers me.\'94 She confessed, her pulse now increasing dramatically and sweat appearing at her brow.\
\'93Yes, I can see that. Baby Richard, you don\'92t mind if I give him a name, do you? He\'92s under stress right now. You must reduce your level of anxiety.\'94\
\'93Are you kidding? How can I be calm when I have been allocated to Alexander Shakti?\'94\
\'93Good point. I would have thrown a rope over a beam, quick smart. I can\'92t imagine your anguish, but Richard\'92s health is paramount. Let\'92s take a look at him then.\'94 She passed her hand over the med-device and a three dimensional depiction of the child appeared in the air above the imaging emitter and floated in the space before them. She spun the image, sliced it through and examined each bodily system and organ in much detail. \'93So far, I cannot see any abnormalities with him. Internal organs and brain structures are completely normal, maybe forming a little quicker than average, but within acceptable norms. Heart strong, nocturnal tachycardia notwithstanding.\'94\
\'93Thank you. Your visits really put my mind at rest.\'94 She did not say that her relaxed state only lasts until Dr Logan leaves. \
\'93So when is the allocation ceremony?\'94\
\'93Tomorrow evening. I haven\'92t even bothered sending out invitations, I am far too embarrassed.\'94 Sarah\'92s mood darkened when she put her mind to the looming allocation. \'93It is a terrible thing to say, but I am so glad all of my family are dead. I could not face them. You can come along and bring Cracker and Hayley if you want.\'94 Tears began welling up in her eyes.\
\'93You will need someone in your corner and I would be honoured to attend. Cracker is level two so he can\'92t go, besides, he can\'92t show his face in public at the moment, you know, being dead and everything. I think I can drag Hayley along, though.\'94 Dead or alive, Cracker would not be among the guests. There was no way he could bring himself to watch Sarah\'92s allocation to someone else, let alone to the biggest idiot in the entire Dominion. \'93Where and when?\'94\
\'93St Branson\'92s of the Immaculate Assets, 5.00pm.\'94 The melancholy tone was unmistakable. \'93It\'92s in Bloomberg Square,you know, opposite the statue of Zuckerberg the Redeemer.\'94\
\'93Have you got a dress?\'94 Every girl wanted a nice dress for their allocation day.\uc0\u8232 \
\'93Second hand! I have the distinct honour of wearing the very same dress Eloise wore at her wedding. She thinks it is some sort of heirloom.\'94 Yet another humiliation. \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

