\f4\fs26 \'93Dearly bejewelled, we are gathered here today to witness the contract exchange of these counter-parties in the matter of holy arbitrage and allocation of Sarah Jacobsen and Alexander Shakti. In praise of the economy we celebrate this allocation of Alexander and Sarah. In the name of the market, the investment and the bottom line.\'94 Spake the Business Theology Manager.\
\'93Money be with you.\'94 All in the temple, eyes glued to the order of ceremony, replied in union.\
\'93Almighty cash, hear our plea for Sarah and Alexander who have come here today to be united in the sacrament of allocation. As their bank accounts join and their assets become one, make them financially stable to increase their faith in each other and the economy.\'94\
\'93May your taxes be small and your profits large.\'94 All parroted from the cheat sheet.\
\'93I now read from the book of Gates, 3:23. An it came to pass that St Murdoch, was in repose in his modest mansion when three tax collectors visited. They said unto him \'91Pay thy fair share of taxation for your accountants are unable to hide your assets. Render unto the exchequer.\'92 St Murdoch replied, \'91I will not, for I am wealthy and can dick you around in court for as long as I like. Furthermore, I shall litigate and ye shall render unto me.\'92 So sayeth the word and the word is money.\'94 The Theology Manager closed the Holy Business Text and kissed it lightly. \'93If anyone here today holds any option over either counter-party, let them settle now or forever hold their peace.\
\'93May your portfolio be fat and your assets hidden.\'94 Refrained the gathering.\
\'93Sarah and Alexander, you have been chosen so that you may seal and harden your resolve for profit. Your union will be strengthened to keep a mutual and lasting faith in each other to carry out the duties of allocation. In the presence of this congregation, I ask you to state you intentions. Sarah and Alexander were you brought here by the devine randomness of allocation?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94 They both said. \
\'93Will you accept your children as gifts from the market and bring them up according to the tenets of business management theory?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94 Said a lone Shakti. \
\'93Sarah?\'94\
\'93Yes, sorry.\'94\
\'93Alexander, please say after me. I, Alexander Caesar Shakti, take you Sarah Elaine Jacobson to be my lawfully contracted allocated female partner. I promise to create wealth enough to increase our social standing, for richer or filthy richer, as long as we both shall hedge.\'94\
\'93I, Alexander Caesar Shakti, take you Sarah Elaine Jacobson to be my lawfully contracted allocated female partner. I promise to create wealth enough to increase our social standing, for richer or filthy richer, as long as we both shall hedge.\'94\
\'93Now you, Sarah. Please say after me. I, Sarah Elaine Jacobson, take you Alexander Caesar Shakti to be my allocated male partner. I promise to create wealth enough to increase our social standing, for richer or filthy richer as long as we both shall hedge.\'94\
 \'93I, Sarah Elaine Jacobson, take you Alexander Caesar Shakti to be my lawfully contracted allocated male partner. I promise to create wealth enough to increase our social standing for richer or filthy richer, as long as we both shall hedge.\'94\
\'93You have declared your consent in this place, before your shareholders and debtors, to be male and female allocated partners. May the market in its infinite wisdom strengthen your consent and fill you with profitability. What the market has brought together, let no-one separate.\'94\
\'93May the market bless this union.\'94 Echoed around the temple.\
\'93Now the exchange of cheques. Let these cheques be a symbol of the deep and contractual nature of this union.\'94\
\'93Take this cheque as a symbol of my investment in this contract.\'94 Alexander was out of the starting blocks immediately.\
After a pregnant pause, Sarah handed a small slip of poly-paper to Alexander, \'93Take this cheque as a symbol of my investment in this contract.\'94\
 \'93Let the cheques be cashed!\'94 The Theology Manager shouted with delight as Sarah and Alexander carefully folded the cheques and placed them in gold wallets, \'93I now pronounce you male and female allocated partners. You may kiss your partner.\'94\
When Shakti lifted the black veil to reveal her perfect face, all present held their breaths in collective awe. She had succumbed to pressure and let the beautician have her way and it had been a spectacular success. Shakti began to shake, but manged to lean in and peck her lips and the small group clapped enthusiastically.\
The reception was held in the sumptuous Warren Buffett Buffet on the top floor of Hardy Tower One, in the most opulent and expensive restaurant in the world, Gravity Well. The food was average and portions tiny, but very pretty, plonked at the of enormous white plates. The ambiance under the gigantic glass dome was simply unbelievable. As the strange coloured light danced about, Sarah\'92s melancholy stared chanced upon a waiter standing in a darkened corner. He was wearing the worst example of a male wig and was scratching at it madly. 
\f5\i Why can\'92t men age with dignity? Then again, I can\'92t talk, my face is covered in paint. 
\f4\i0 He rotated the head piece almost back into place and then took a bee-line straight towards her. As he approached, his gait and stride were reminiscent of someone she knew. C
\f5\i racker!
\f4\i0 \
\'93Would the blushing female allocated partner like a beverage?\'94 Cracker asked with as much dignity as the wig allowed.\
\'93I am so glad to see you. How did you\'85..?\'94 Sarah beamed light.\
\'93I know people in low places. Don\'92t you know who is playing tonight? The High Elvis himself. He\'92ll be incognito, though. He\'92ll be in disguised as Elvis.\'94 They both laughed, but cut it short when she felt the disapproving eye of her mother-in-law. \
\'93Better than your disguise.\'94 For the sake of appearances, she bit down on a chuckle. \'93What if Alexander recognises you?\'94\
\'93He won\'92t.\'94 Cracker knew Shakti would be completely distracted by Sarah.\
\'93I hope you haven\'92t got any gags lined up. Exploding cake, perhaps?\'94\
\'93There is no need. I just have to stand back and watch Shakti fuck up. He\'92s bound to do something stupid.\'94\
\'93I hope not. I get the impression his mother is not the forgiving type.\'94\
\'93Here\'92s something that\'92s weird. Check out the man sitting two down from dear old mother Shakti. Recognise him?\'94 Cracker was cryptic, but clearly amused.\
\'93Yes, that\'92s your friend Halo, isn\'92t it?\
\'93The very same. According to the seating chart he is Haloren Smythe, Director, L.6.\'94\
\'93L.6? What is he doing here?\'94\
\'93I don\'92t think that is the right question. He is not out of place here. Why was he hanging out with me and my dubious friends?\'94\
\'93I don\'92t think we will find out tonight.\'94\
\'93The High Elvis isn\'92t here just to play a few songs. He wants to congratulate you in behalf of the Elvi and get a couple of photos. It\'92s good P.R.\'94 Cracker whispered. \'93Champagne? Of course, madam.\'94 He scuttled away and disappeared into the kitchen. \
\'93It was good to see you smile, Sarah.\'94 Shakti said, leaning into her right ear.\
\'93Oh, you frightened me! Goodness.\'94 Sarah laid her hands protectively upon her stomach and tried another smile.\
\'93That\'92s better. I have noticed you don\'92t look happy. Sarah, I am perfectly aware of what I am and truly honoured that you would let me breath the same air as you, let alone agree to allocation. You must know how beautiful you are and getting stuck with me must be greatly disappointing.\'94 His eyes fell to the floor and he fought off tears.\
\'93Alex, we have exchanged cheques.\'94 She touched his face gently and decided to fake it for the rest of the evening. \'93I haven\'92t been feeling well lately, a little nauseous that\'92s all.\'94 \
\'93Nauseous? Are you okay?\'94\
 \'93I am fine.\'94 She didn\'92t want to have that conversation yet.\
\'93Are you feeling well enough to cut the cake?\'94\
\'93We should have speeches first, but if you want to cut the cake, we shall cut the cake, husband.\'94 The word nearly choked her, but she saw it made him immensely happy. She thought to kiss him, but was too repulsed by the prospect.\
\'93I have made sure the knife is sharp and it will be slightly heated so it will slice through the cake smooth as silk and there will be hardly any crumbs.\'94 Shakti smiled. He had really put some thought into the cake cutting ceremony and was proud of himself. No-one else would think of that!\
The small crowd gathered around a round table located in the centre of the restaurant, directly under the glass dome as pink and green auroras performed aerial gymnastics above. The pure white, three tiered cake took honoured position in the centre of the table and stood before Sarah and Shakti awaiting symbolic penetration. They both held the knife and without word or ceremony, plunged it into the heart of the extravagant gateau. As they received polite claps and a few hoorah\'92s and Sarah dutifully handed Alexander the first piece of cake. He bowed in deference and raised the cake to his mouth with his right hand, the same hand that held the knife. He stabbed himself in the eye and screamed, his arms flailed about and as Sarah stepped in to assist him, the knife poked shallowly into her throat, just sufficiently to severe her carotid artery. The crowd reeled back, screaming and yelling, but Cracker was by Sarah\'92s side in a second, applying direct pressure, but she quickly faded into unconsciousness.\
\'93Will someone stop him please? He\'92s going to stab someone else\'94 Cracker yelled out, but know one seemed to listen until he saw his colleagues, Detective Chief Superintendent Hayley Lanning and Dr Kathy Logan step up. \
\'93He barely scratched the cornea. He\'92ll be fine.\'94 Kathy said, peeling off her patch. \'93Let me see, sir.\'94\
\'93It\'92s me.\'94 Cracker said,\
\'93I know.\'94 She said gravely, \'93That is the worst disguise ever. It looks like the artery has been severed. I will have to do a little surgery right here.\'94\
\'93Madam. We have a small first aid room. The light is better there.\'94 The maitre d\'92 suggested over her shoulder. He was running a restaurant and vascular surgery does not make for good ambiance. \
Sarah was frantically carried through the foyer and into a small, but most certainly well lit room with an examination table, a first aid kit and a small sink. \'93The severed ends of the artery have might have retracted. I\'92ll have to find them and and pull them back together. She flushed the wound clear and placed her fingers inside to dig about but miraculously the artery had not retracted, but was in perfect position to apply the glue. \
\'93Cracker hand me the suture kit.\'94 Kathy asked quietly as she continue to apply pressure to the wound. She gradually reduced the pressure, waiting for it to gush, but it did not. She removed her fingers completely and it did not bleed at all. The artery had re-attached and the sliced tissue melded back into one when she pressed the skin tightly together. \'93I don\'92t think I will need to glue this.\'94\
The repaired artery was now allowing oxygenated blood to the brain and within a couple of minutes Sarah had regained consciousness.\
\'93I told you he would do something stupid.\'94 Cracker laughed at the blood splattered bride, helping her to her feet. \'93You heal fast as well, huh? That disc must have had some magic shit in it.\'94\
\'93Yes, it must have. Lucky for us both, now.\'94 She vacantly replied and she stared at herself in the mirror. Her fingers gently caressing the bright red cut in the left side of her neck. \'93I am glad we have a tradition of black wedding gowns, my goodness can you imagine a white dress? Look, I will be fine. Tell them to mop the floor for the allocation waltz and I will wash up and be out in five minutes.\'94\
The door of the small room burst open and a petite dignified woman gracefully stepped inside. Eloise had seen the amount of blood that spilled out and calculated Sarah would have insufficient blood left to sustain life. She wanted to confirm the death so she could get on with seizing her assets. Sarah had a nice little portfolio and it would fatten up Alex\'92s nest egg considerably. \
 \'93Where is my dear daughter?\'94 Mother Shakti said, but was immediately stunned by the unlikely state of Sarah. She was breathing and standing upright. \'93My dear, I thought you to be dead.\'94\
\'93No such luck, Eloise.\'94 She smiled. \'93Are we ready to return to the reception?\'94\
\'93Most of the guests have gone home.\'94 Eloise did not invite anyone too important and would not suffer too much embarrassment following the wedding cake fiasco. At least she wasn\'92t going to spend the night protecting her idiot son from a manslaughter charge. Stabbing a bride to death at a wedding will alway raise a few questions, no matter what your social status.\
\'93No speeches then? Good.\'94 Sarah was glad the night was moving along fast. \'93How is Alexander?\'94\
\'93He sliced the corner of his eye and scratched the cornea. There was not much blood. Unfortunately for us all, he is going to survive.\'94 Eloise smiled and looked to laugh, but her grin faded.\
\'93That\'92s my husband your are talking about.\'94 Sarah laughed and walked out the door. Eloise grunted and followed.\
It was during the allocation dance, when they were up close that Sarah thought to tell him the happy news. \'93Alexander, I am pregnant.\'94\
\'93That is wonderful news, wonderful. I am so happy.\'94 Said Long-John Shakti, looking ridiculous in an eye patch.\
\'93I told you I haven\'92t been feeling well, right? My doctor said, just to be on the safe side, we shouldn\'92t have sex until the child is born.\'94\
\'93What?\'94\
\'93Doctor\'92s orders, husband.\'94 She choked on the lie and from saying that husband word again.\
\'93Anything for you, my wife.\'94 Alex whispered in her ear. She began to cough loudly and had to separate from him. \
\'93Let\'92s sit down.\'94 
\f5\i Wife? Tax me fully!
\f4\i0 \
\'93I\'92ve got to got and tell mother the good news\'94\
\'93What news?\'94\uc0\u8232 \
\'93You\'92re pregnant. Have you forgotten already?\'94 Shakti skipped off to his mother who feigned delight as they hugged. She looked over her son\'92s shoulder and winked at Sarah. She did not wink back. She was not cool with lying and she had set herself up for a lifelong deception.\
\'93I didn\'92t think you would go through with it. Shakti, what a joke.\'94 The Johnny was angry and drunk.\
\'93Oh, Johnny, just give me a hug and be happy for me. Someone has to be.\'94 They hugged uncomfortably, like two strangers. \'93I heard you blew up the lab.\'94 She hope to lighten the mood.\
\'93Yes. So what? Why do you want to embarrass me? Do you want to see the holographs so you can get a visual of my humiliation?\'94 He lumbered out his hand device and was quickly scrolling through holographs of the lab. \
\'93Wait! Go back.\'94 Sarah was breathing became instantly laboured and her heart was in her mouth. \'93Yes. That one.\'94 She looked at the interior of the damaged lab. Through the water damage and the soot she could clearly see a distinct pattern. The manner in which the blue electric arcs had struck the walls was undeniably the same pattern as she had been dreaming of for weeks. \'93Send me a copy, now.\'94\
\'93Okay.\'94 His swiped his had across the device and the image was sent.\
\'93Don\'92t get too comfortable, pal.\'94 The waiter said to Johnny from behind.\
\'93How dare you, you low-life scum! You, you\'85 level one waiter!\'94 As he yelled Cracker raised his wig and took off a fake nose. \'93I thought you were dead. I should have known it was too good to be true.\'94\
\'93Alive and kicking.\'94 Cracker smiled returning the wig to its original silly position.\
\'93Damn it, this night just keeps getting worse.\'94 The Johnny stomped off to the bar, but was refused service by a low-life level one bartender with great hearing.\
\'93The High Elvis needs to speak to you after this set.\'94 Cracker whispered to Sarah.\
\'93Okay, do you know where Kathy is? I need to speak with her.\'94\
\'93I think she is on the floor over behind the fountain. She\'92ll be back with us soon.\'94\
Sarah could not wait and dashed over to the fountain to find Kathy waking from a knock-out hit of THC-acetate. \'93Kathy? Kathy?\'94 She looked at Sarah but did not respond. \'93Dr Logan to reception. Dr Logan please come to reception. Hello?\'94\
\'93Huh? Wow that was intense! What\'92s up?\'94 Dr Logan rose slowly to her feet, the image of the lab presented before her. \'93A bit of a mess.\'94\
\'93Its the inside of the lab Johnny blew up. See the pattern of damage?\'94\
\'93Seems random to me.\'94\
\'93It is exactly the same pattern as the one I have been dreaming about. I am certain of it.\'94 She ran an index finger over the screen, slowly and carefully tracing the burn marks on the wall and floor, then pressed an icon at the bottom of the screen, causing the image to drop away, leaving only the trace marks. \'93I probably won\'92t be available for a couple of days, so could you do some research on this pattern. I need to know what it means.\'94\
\'93Sure thing Mrs Shakti.\'94 Kathy thought to try Sarah\'92s new title on for size.\
\'93Oh, that hurts. I think I prefer Holy Mother.\'94 She quietly joked as she hugged Kathy tight. \'93I\'92ve got to go and speak with the High Elvis, now.\'94 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

