\f4\fs26 \'93Cracker? Can we speak?\'94 Hayley Lanning sidled up from the rear.\
\'93I am a waiter.\'94 Cracker said looking in the other direction.\
\'93I don\'92t think anyone is falling for it. Do you know who that man is? The one sitting at the bar by himself.\'94\
\'93Haloren Smythe, Company Director, L.6.\'94 Cracker replied.\
\'93Level 6. You don\'92t see many of those around. Getting to level 6 takes serious money or serious corruption, usually a combination of both.\'94 Hayley had never been impressed by any level 6 snob and just knew this guy was cut from the same cloth.\
\'93I\'92ve met him heaps of times, in fact he was a part of my group of friends, but thinking back I can\'92t remember who introduced him to the group. He just seemed to appear a few years ago and attached himself to us. We all used to meet for drinks regularly, but it was pretty obvious he wasn\'92t that interested in speaking with us. His only concern was picking up and getting out as quickly as possible.\'94 Crackers recalled with a curious frown across his brow.\
\'93A level 6 Company Director with a alter-ego as a Level 2 pick up artist. Very unusual indeed. I noticed him when Sarah was bleeding all over the floor. He was staring at the blood and smiling. I swear he was about to laugh.\'94 Hayley shook her head in disgust. \'93And he has been staring at you, I think with surprise, but it could be something more sinister.\'94 Hayley\'92s internal alarm was ringing loudly in her head, red flags flapping madly.\
\'93That doesn\'92t surprise me, he is very intense and has a dark sense of humour, I mean pitch black. I lost count of the number of times he said \'91All level one\'92s must die.\'92 He\'92s one extremely cold guy and takes himself very, very seriously.\'94 Cracker liked him, but always knew not to cross him. \'93Sarah told me he has retinal enhancements with some sort of vid-screen grafted onto his corneas. According to her that was the secret of his success with women.\'94 \
\'93How are you feeling about all this?\'94 She saw how he looked at Sarah and it was obvious, to any casual observer, that his was infatuated. Hayley did not like aspirational lows and he was aiming far too high.\
\'93Not happy at all, in fact I have been fighting back tears all night. I could fall into a depression or act out with anger, but what would that achieve? I am certain Sarah would find that unacceptable. I have to face reality, I am Level 2 and she is level 5.\'94 \
\'93It is good you understand the limitations of your low status.\'94 She was deliberately cruel. Weddings always made Hayley depressed and angry, something of which she was completely unaware. 
\f5\i Level 2\'92s must know their place. The Great Teacher indeed!
\f4\i0 \
\'93Yeah, thanks for that. I really appreciate your support.\'94 Cracker felt the burn and decided on an exit strategy. \'93It looks like the High Elvis is finishing up his last set. I will have to fetch Sarah.\'94 Hayley\'92s broadside had hit him as hard, as she had intended, but this only served to increase his resolve. One day he hoped to live in dignity, something that people like Hayley would always strive to deny him. \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

