\f4\fs26 It took Cracker no time to locate Sarah and the High Elvis chatting intently backstage in the Green Room and he left them to it. Pleased he had finally managed to get the High Elvis and The Holy Mother together, he slithered back into the banquet hall and kept close to the walls. Trying to stay out of Haloren\'92s line of sight, as he made good his escape, he vacantly slid behind a mammoth set of drapes, obscuring a polished stone wall. As he sidled closer a small section began to shimmer, then coalesce into a glistening metal door. It opened automatically and Cracker poked his head in, assuming it was a back door to the kitchen or a maybe a fire-exit, but seeing neither stairs or knife wielding chefs, he walked in. He heard the door close behind him and turned to see that, from this side, the door was transparent. Touching the door with his hand caused the door to automatically open and when he backed away, it closed again. 
\f5\i Cool, I\'92m not locked in.
\f4\i0 \
He spun around and found himself in a darkened room, the only light filtering in through the door and another similar door 10 metres to his left. In the dimness he stumbled across what he thought to be a console, but it had buttons and no back-light. He took a punt and gingerly pressed a button or three until the room illuminated to reveal a huge control room, appointed with old computers, monitors and other machines that he could not identify. Too scared to touch anything else, he returned to the reception and promptly located Kathy stumbling about on the dance floor.\
\'93Hey Kathy, walk behind those drapes over there.\'94 Cracker pointed.\
\'93I am not so intoxicated as to fall for that one, sir.\'94 Kathy wagged her index finger and shook her head.\
\'93I am not kidding. Just walk behind those drapes. It\'92s worth it.\'94\
\'93Okay.\'94 A bemused Dr Logan walked over to the drapes and looked behind them. Nothing but a straight line of uninspiring stone wall. She began to walk back, but Cracker shook his head and against her better judgment she disappeared behind the curtains and re-appeared at the other end. \'93Very funny. What\'92s the joke?\'94 \
\'93I don\'92t understand.\'94 He took her by the arm and as they entered the space behind the curtains, the door began to appear before them. \'93You see that, don\'92t you?\'94\
\'93Yes, but that didn\'92t happen for me.\'94 She was now enthralled and entered without hesitation. \'93What\'92s in here?\'94 \
\'93I don\'92t know. I think it may be an old office or control room. Look at all the old computers, they must be really old. It doesn\'92t look like anything has been used in years.\'94\
