\f4\fs26  Sarah dropped in to see Kathy at the morgue as soon as she had returned from her honeymoon. Honeymoon was probably overstating the significance of her break from work. She was pleased that Shakti had not once tried anything with her the entire time, having taken her doctor\'92s advice to heart. \
\'93Holy Mother, I am happy to see you!\'94 Kathy gushed and gave her a long and uncomfortable long hug. \
\'93I am getting used to Mrs Shakti, but bless you.\'94 Sarah replied. \'93What of the damage pattern?\'94 As soon as she turned her mind to the pattern, it popped into her mind in perfect clarity. She pressed down on the distress the image caused and held her stomach gently.\
\'93Okay, I have researched that pattern as much as I can. I found many possible matches. Come in, and have a look. For example, this Jackson Pollack painting, when viewed with infra-red light, there is an 90% match in this area here. This massive constellation in the Hancock galaxy, Rinehardt\'92s Caboose, is an 80% match. There is one ancient civilisation from Equatorial Britain that used this icon as a symbol of knowledge and destruction. It is about an 85% match, but if you alter the perspective and look at it from an angle of 23 degrees, the match becomes 96%.\'94\
\'93That one sounds promising. Why 23 degrees?\'94\
\'93I don\'92t know exactly. Maybe the tilt in the earth\'92s axis? I tried it from every different angle, 23 degrees was the closest match.\'94\
\'93Any others?\'94\
\'93Quite a few. This one is a 98 % match without changing perspectives. It is called a Beta-mode identifier pattern. It is the pattern left by the gravity waves released at the moment of the big bang. Gravity waves were emitted even before light existed, so cool! It is like looking back in time, almost back to the beginning of time itself.\'94 \
At that moment Sarah felt the accumulation of anxiety and fear that had recently piled up, wash away in a cleansing shower for her soul. The sick feeling in her stomach ceased immediately and she felt it replaced by a warm contented glow. \'93That\'92s it. Stop now. I am certain.\'94\
\'93Why would you be freaking out about a beta-mode identifier pattern? It\'92s pretty obscure.\'94 \
\'93I don\'92t know, but there is an obvious link. The damage pattern was caused by a Gyges Disc and it is believed they are powered by gravity waves. Can you send Johnny all of your data? He might find it interesting.\'94
